From: pzl8-nss project
Subject: [PATCH] nss_core: make file-local helpers static

nss_core_handle_nss_status_pkt() and nss_skb_reuse() are only referenced
from nss_core.c and are not exported, but were defined with external
linkage and no prototype. OpenWrt builds the kernel with
-Wmissing-prototypes (scripts/Makefile.extrawarn) escalated to an error,
so this breaks the build on 6.12. Give both functions internal linkage.

Signed-off-by: pzl8-nss
---
--- a/nss_core.c
+++ b/nss_core.c
@@ -401,7 +401,7 @@
  * nss_core_handle_nss_status_pkt()
  *	Handle the metadata/status packet.
  */
-void nss_core_handle_nss_status_pkt(struct nss_ctx_instance *nss_ctx, struct sk_buff *nbuf)
+static void nss_core_handle_nss_status_pkt(struct nss_ctx_instance *nss_ctx, struct sk_buff *nbuf)
 {
 	struct nss_cmn_msg *ncm;
 	uint32_t expected_version = NSS_HLOS_MESSAGE_VERSION;
@@ -2850,7 +2850,7 @@
  * NOTE: This function does any necessary reference count dropping, and
  * cleans up the skbuff as if its allocated fresh.
  */
-void nss_skb_reuse(struct sk_buff *nbuf)
+static void nss_skb_reuse(struct sk_buff *nbuf)
 {
 	struct skb_shared_info *shinfo;
 
